    Auto-encode audio track for Whisper (#6248)
    
    Whisper.cpp requires a very specific input audio format. Instead of
    relying on adopters working around this in the workflow and encoding
    tracks in advance, this patch includes the encoding in the operation
    itself.
    
    This not only has the advantage that the configuration is much easier,
    but it also means that only the tracks selected to actually be used for
    generating the subtitles are encoded.
    
    ### How to test this patch
    
    Configure Whisper.ccp and add the `speechtotext` operation to the fast
    testing workflow:
    
    ```yaml
      - id: speechtotext
        description: Generates subtitles for video and audio files
        configurations:
          - source-flavor: '*/source'
          - target-flavor: captions/source
          - target-tags: engage-download
          - target-flavor: captions/source
          - limit-to-one: true
    ```
    
    If you now ingest an `.mp4` file, the operation should be able to work
    on it.
    
